Model a Worker Who Waits for a Free Target
You can model two Workers who pick parts up from a Workplace attached to a Source.
The Workers 
  then carry the parts to a Workplace attached to the entrance of the ParallelStation, and
place them onto one of the four processing places. Once all processing places are stocked with parts, the
Workers walk around the ParallelStation to the Workplace attached to its exit. They finally pick a processed
part up and place it onto the Workplace attached to the Conveyor.
The finished simulation model looks like this:
Model a Worker Who Waits for a Free Target
10-464 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Proceed as follows to create the simulation model:
• Insert the two Sources. We used them with their default settings.
Make sure that Wait for Free Target on the tab Importer > sub-tab Transport is turned on. This
prevents that a Worker is requested if the target is not free. A Worker only walks to the station on which
the part is located once the target is free. He then picks the part up and carries it to the target.
• Insert a Workplace 
  next to each of the Sources where the Workers picks up the parts. Drag the
Workplace close to one of the sides of Source, which you want to use as the Station.
Model a Worker Who Waits for a Free Target
Plant Simulation Help 10-465
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Plant Simulation then
◦ Opens a window asking you if you want to activate a required importer, a Transport Importer in our
case. Click the button to activate it.
◦ Enters the Source as the Station into the Workplace.
◦ Selects the check boxes At Entrance and At Exit of the Workplace.
The Workers carry the produced parts to the Workplace attached to the entrance of the
ParallelStation and place them there.
They pick the processed parts up at the Workplace attached to the exit of the ParallelStation.
• Insert the ParallelStation that processes a part on each of its four processing places.
Insert a Workplace close to the left side of the ParallelStation where the Workers place the part. Drag
the Workplace to the ParallelStation.
Plant Simulation then
◦ Opens a window asking you if you want to activate a required importer, a Transport Importer in our
case. Click Transport Importer to activate it.
◦ Enters the ParallelStation as the Station into the Workplace.
◦ Selects the check boxes At Entrance and At Exit of the Workplace.
As we want this Workplace to be at the entrance of the ParallelStation, we clear At Exit.
Model a Worker Who Waits for a Free Target
10-466 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The Workers carry the produced parts to the Workplace attached to the entrance of the
ParallelStation.
• Insert a Workplace close to the right side of the ParallelStation where the Workers pick up the parts to
carry them to the Conveyor. This enters the ParallelStation as the Station into the Workplace and selects
the check boxes At Entrance and At Exit.
As we want this Workplace to be at the exit of the ParallelStation, we clear At Entrance.
The Workers pick the processed parts up at the Workplace attached to the exit of the ParallelStation.
• Configure the ParallelStation.
◦ We entered a Processing Time of 5 seconds
◦ Make sure that Wait for Free Target on the tab Importer > sub-tab Transport is turned on. This
prevents that a Worker is requested if the target is not free. A Worker only walks to the station on
which the part is located once the target is free. He then picks the part up and carries it to the target.
• Insert a Conveyor. Our Conveyor has these settings.
Model a Worker Who Waits for a Free Target
