Plant Simulation automatically enters the Exporters and the services into the Broker which we
specified. To view them, open MyBroker and select View > Exporters and View > Offered Services.
• Finally, open the EventController and click Start/Stop Simulation. As the Exporters can only work at
one station at a time, and because the stations Station1 and Station3 share the ExporterJob1, short
standstills occur. Station1 has to wait until Station3 releases ExporterJob1, and thus is blocked. Station3
in turn has to wait until Station1 releases ExporterJob1, and thus is Waiting.
You can also click the tab Statistics and view the most important data, which the object collected.
Back to Model Workers with Importer, Broker, and Exporter
Model Processing and Set-up Jobs
You an model jobs, which process parts and which set the station up to process these different types of
parts.
The Exporter provides the services, while the Broker assigns the Exporter to the station, which we here
model with the object Station. All stations need the service named Setup, which Exporter3 provides,
for setting the station up for a new part type. Station1 and Station3 both require the Exporter named
Exporter1, which provides the services Job1 and Job2. The station Station2 requires the service Job2,
which Exporter2 provides.
To model this, we proceed like this:
• Insert a Source, three Stations, and a Drain. Connect them. Then, insert three Exporters, a Broker,
and a table, which contains the products. Finally, insert a Method, name it reset, and enter
deleteMovables as source code.
Model Processing and Set-up Jobs
